360
00:13:41,369 --> 00:13:43,865
Now divide that by the miles.

361
00:13:44,045 --> 00:13:46,820
If an owner drives three thousand miles

362
00:13:46,820 --> 00:13:49,881
a year, thirty-one thousand five hundred to

363
00:13:49,881 --> 00:13:53,083
fifty-six thousand dollars works out to about

364
00:13:53,083 --> 00:13:56,144
ten dollars fifty cents to eighteen dollars

365
00:13:56,144 --> 00:13:57,781
seventy cents per mile,

366
00:13:57,781 --> 00:13:59,347
by our own arithmetic.

367
00:13:59,527 --> 00:14:01,852
Every trip to the grocery store in

368
00:14:01,852 --> 00:14:03,698
a Ford GT costs more than a

369
00:14:03,698 --> 00:14:04,519
nice dinner.

370
00:14:04,869 --> 00:14:05,908
Over five years,

371
00:14:05,908 --> 00:14:08,702
that would be about one hundred fifty-seven

372
00:14:08,702 --> 00:14:11,821
thousand to two hundred eighty thousand dollars,

373
00:14:11,821 --> 00:14:13,251
by our own arithmetic.

374
00:14:13,431 --> 00:14:15,491
On top of a purchase price of

375
00:14:15,491 --> 00:14:17,053
around half a million.

376
00:14:17,233 --> 00:14:19,985
So a five-year Ford GT experience could

377
00:14:19,985 --> 00:14:23,159
involve roughly six hundred fifty thousand to

378
00:14:23,159 --> 00:14:26,687
seven hundred eighty thousand dollars of spending,

379
00:14:26,687 --> 00:14:28,309
before selling the car.

380
00:14:28,660 --> 00:14:30,690
And measured against income,

381
00:14:30,690 --> 00:14:33,519
those five years of running costs alone

382
00:14:33,519 --> 00:14:35,695
equal about two to three and a

383
00:14:35,695 --> 00:14:38,813
half years of the median American household

384
00:14:38,813 --> 00:14:40,989
income, by our own arithmetic.

385
00:14:41,169 --> 00:14:43,639
That is before the purchase price,

386
00:14:43,639 --> 00:14:46,836
before taxes, and before any surprise repair

387
00:14:46,836 --> 00:14:48,797
on a carbon fiber supercar.

388
00:14:49,147 --> 00:14:50,865
But here is the twist again.

389
00:14:51,045 --> 00:14:53,116
If the car is then worth about

390
00:14:53,116 --> 00:14:56,154
seven hundred eighty-eight thousand dollars,

391
00:14:56,154 --> 00:14:59,883
as Hagerty's valuation suggested in twenty twenty-six,

392
00:14:59,883 --> 00:15:02,093
the owner could get much of that

393
00:15:02,093 --> 00:15:02,852
money back.

394
00:15:03,032 --> 00:15:05,054
The real cost of a Ford GT

395
00:15:05,054 --> 00:15:07,931
depends almost entirely on what it is

396
00:15:07,931 --> 00:15:09,720
